      "writtenOn": "2022-08-19T16:31:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here and below, you can keep things much more local. For example, use:\n\n```\n#include \u003czephyr/fff.h\u003e\n\nDEFINE_FFF_GLOBALS;\n\nFAKE_VALUE_FUNC(const uint32_t *const, pd_get_src_caps, int);\n\n/* In your suite\u0027s \u0027before\u0027 function you\u0027ll need to call\n * RESET_FAKE(pd_get_src_caps);\n * FFF_RESET_HISTORY();\n */\n \n/* In your test... */\nZTEST(...)\n{\n  const uint32_t mock_pd_src_pdo[] \u003d {\n    PDO_FIXED(5000, 1500, PDO_FIXED_FLAGS),\n  };\n  pd_get_src_caps_fake.return_value \u003d mock_pd_src_pdo;\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nThe above lets you keep the mock values local to your test and also assert on the mocked functions if needed/desired",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "193c1abc22b7370228946211d3ca7004e817636d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
